{
  "name": "Avoiding Common Custom Framing Mistakes",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "It's easy to get excited about custom framing, but a few common missteps can really mess things up. One of the biggest mistakes we see is inaccurate measurements. You might think you've got it, but mismeasuring your artwork can lead to wasted materials and costly redos. Then there’s the issue of skipping written approvals; it’s super important to have everything documented so there are no surprises down the line. Another big one is mishandling the artwork itself. Some pieces are delicate or irreplaceable, and one wrong move can cause permanent damage. That's why we always recommend working with folks who know how to properly handle and frame your treasures. We've seen it all, from miscut glass to ordering the wrong quantity of molding, and it all adds up to delays and frustration. To avoid these headaches, start with a clear idea of what you want and where the piece will hang. Discuss your style preferences, glass choices, and matting options during the consultation. And always confirm measurements and design details before any cutting begins. When your piece is valuable, unusually shaped, or requires specialized treatment like shadow boxes or unique glazing, it’s definitely worth bringing in a professional. We can help you navigate the process, ensuring your artwork is protected and beautifully displayed without any costly blunders.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
